    "finalAnswer": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "- **Cause:** Standalone assembly copied Palace’s runtime but omitted transitive public declaration dependencies. Thus `plugin.d.ts` could not resolve `../../platform/plugin-contract.js`, the missing declaration link behind the `PluginContext` issue. The recorded Windows failure is in `source-traces/01-public-types-red.log`; the cause is documented in `source-traces/incident.md`.\n\n- **Fix:** At build time, use TypeScript’s parser and NodeNext resolver to recursively copy the exact canonical `.d.ts` dependencies, then verify that runtime and declaration imports stay inside the package and reject unreviewed computed imports. The implementation is in `source-traces/03-closure-implementation.mjs`, integrated by `source-traces/05-standalone-builder.mjs`. It preserves the public plugin export and adds no MCP Device runtime dependency.\n\n- **Independent checks:** `source-traces/04-independent-closure-check.test.mjs` independently traverses the exported declaration graph and checks package containment. It also tests escaping imports, import-like comments/strings, and unreviewed computed imports. `source-traces/02-public-types-and-closure-green.log` records **all four passing**, versus the original **one failing** check. These are recorded results, not a fresh rerun.\n\n**Reusable procedure:** No genuinely validated procedure is available in this Palace runtime: `palace skills` returned none, including candidates. The selected card is only `observed`, and `source-traces/incident.md` explicitly says these observations are **not a validated reusable procedure**.\n\nI read the selected card and all six original source-trace files; I made no changes."
      }
